From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: Print Screen can open a screenshot app

Dresden, 2026-10-23: people who prefer another screenshot tool (GNOME
Screenshot, Flameshot, Spectacle, ksnip) should be able to have Print
Screen open it. ChromeOS's own screen capture stays the default.

- Settings > Apps > Default apps gets a Screenshots (Print Screen) row:
  ChromeOS's screen capture, or an installed Linux app whose name or
  keywords say it takes screenshots. The choice is the profile pref
  nickel.tools.screenshot (the app's desktop file id; empty for the
  screen capture).
- Ash's snip key command asks the capture mode delegate first. Chrome's
  delegate has nickel-appd start the chosen app
  (org.nickelos.Apps.LaunchTool, kind "screenshot"), which uses the app's
  capture action when it has one (Flameshot's Capture: launched as it is,
  Flameshot only starts its tray icon). If the app can't be started,
  ChromeOS's capture mode opens as before.
- Only the snip key changes: Ctrl+Show windows and the other capture
  shortcuts stay ChromeOS's.

diff --git a/ash/accelerators/accelerator_commands.cc b/ash/accelerators/accelerator_commands.cc
index 3bb8c539f7bfb..1a82584c44773 100644
--- a/ash/accelerators/accelerator_commands.cc
+++ b/ash/accelerators/accelerator_commands.cc
@@ -1289,10 +1289,20 @@ void TakeScreenshot(bool from_snapshot_key) {
   auto* capture_mode_controller = CaptureModeController::Get();
   if (from_snapshot_key &&
       !Shell::Get()->session_controller()->IsUserSessionBlocked()) {
-    if (capture_mode_controller->IsActive())
+    if (capture_mode_controller->IsActive()) {
       capture_mode_controller->Stop();
-    else
-      capture_mode_controller->Start(CaptureModeEntryType::kSnipKey);
+      return;
+    }
+    // NickelOS: the screenshot app chosen in Settings > Apps > Default apps
+    // takes the key instead; capture mode if it can't start.
+    if (capture_mode_controller->NickelLaunchScreenshotTool(
+            base::BindOnce([] {
+              CaptureModeController::Get()->Start(
+                  CaptureModeEntryType::kSnipKey);
+            }))) {
+      return;
+    }
+    capture_mode_controller->Start(CaptureModeEntryType::kSnipKey);
     return;
   }
   capture_mode_controller->CaptureScreenshotsOfAllDisplays();
